title: Right coalition collapses
subtitle: The <span style="color: #000000;">propertied</span>-<span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span> coalition has collapsed...
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: dnf_formed and year = 1928 and month = 11 and center_right_coalition < 50 and in_center_right_coalition and not lvp_formed
max-visits: 1

= Mallin's exit from the coalition

When Mallin established his own party, he successfully attracted a significant number of former <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> Assembly members to join his party and to oppose the current center-right coalition. The current government lacks a majority within the Assembly and may be taken down with a no-confidence vote.

We can either vote to bring down the government and hold new elections, or "tolerate" a government led by the remaining propertied parties. It would be extremely unpopular within our party to support a government that has the participation of the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>—despite their removal of the most extreme factions—would be highly unpopular within our party. 

- @vonc_yes
- @vonc_no  
- @no_matter

@vonc_yes
title: Support the vote of no confidence, voting against the government.
subtitle: The government will collapse, and there will be new elections.
view-if: cordon_sanitaire >= 50 and center_right_coalition < 50
on-arrival: time_to_election = 3; marcher_in_government = 0; in_right_coalition = 0; in_center_right_coalition = 0; in_grand_coalition = 0; marcher_toleration = 0; marcher_toleration_right = 0; pro_republic -= 2; gold_relation -= 4; unionist_relation -= 4; traditionalist_relation -= 4; ddp_relation -= 4; ddp_cohesion -= 1; ddp_right += 1; guild_dnf += 3; landed_dnf += 3
call: set_next_election_time
go-to: new_prussia_election if (in_center_right_coalition_heartland or in_right_coalition_heartland)

The right-wing coalition has fallen. New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year + 2365 +].

@vonc_no
title: Oppose the vote of no confidence, voting for the government.
subtitle: We would essentially provide "toleration" to a propertied government.
view-if: cordon_sanitaire >= 50 and center_right_coalition < 50
choose-if: (reformist_strength >= center_strength + left_strength)
unavailable-subtitle: [? if (center_strength + left_strength >= reformist_strength) : Most of the party is in complete opposition to this. ?]
on-arrival: marcher_toleration = 1; marcher_toleration_right = 1; in_right_coalition = 0; in_center_right_coalition = 1; left_dissent += 30; center_dissent += 25; labor_dissent += 20; reformist_dissent += 10; commons_marcher -= 3; burgher_marcher -= 6; guild_marcher -= 6; landed_marcher -= 4; faithful_marcher -= 5; gold_left += 1; ddp_left += 1; liberal_cooperation += 1; bourgeois_cooperation += 2
go-to: new_prussia_election if (in_center_right_coalition_heartland or in_right_coalition_heartland)

By supporting the government, we have essentially entered into a "toleration" arrangement with the [+ chancellor +] government. We do not have a voice in the government, but we are responsible for its continued stability. This is wildly unpopular within the party and our supporters, as we allowed a right-wing government to form twice now.

@no_matter
title: It does not matter what we do.
subtitle: The anti-government parties have over 50% of the vote, no matter our choices.
view-if: cordon_sanitaire < 50
call: set_next_election_time
on-arrival: time_to_election = 3; marcher_in_government = 0; in_right_coalition = 0; in_grand_coalition = 0; marcher_toleration = 0; marcher_toleration_right = 0; pro_republic -= 5
go-to: new_prussia_election if (in_center_right_coalition_heartland or in_right_coalition_heartland)

The right-wing coalition has fallen. New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year + 2365 +].

@new_prussia_election
on-arrival: heartland_coalition_trigger = 1 if center_right_coalition_heartland < 50

Mallin has also attracted some members of the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> to split into the <span style="color: #003755;">**CNF**</span> in the Heartland state Assembly too, [? if center_right_coalition_heartland < 50 and in_right_coalition_heartland: even if the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> were to join in, they still lack a sufficient majority. ?][? if center_right_coalition_heartland >= 50 and in_right_coalition_heartland: but if the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> were to enter, they would have a governing coalition. ?][? if center_right_coalition_heartland >= 50 and in_center_right_coalition_heartland: but it still isn't enough to deny the ruling coalition a majority. ?][? if center_right_coalition_heartland < 50 and in_center_right_coalition_heartland: and it's enough to deny the ruling coalition a majority. ?]

We have an opportunity to change the composition of the Heartland coalition.


- @prussia_coalition
- @new_prussia_election_oppo: We will stay in opposition.
- @prussian_coalition_formation: Negotiate a new Heartland coalition.
- @new_prussia_election_called: Refuse to form a coalition, so new elections are to be called.

@prussia_coalition
title: Use our resources to convince the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> to reconsider.
subtitle: -1 resources
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources (need 1).
view-if: center_right_coalition_heartland >= 50 and in_right_coalition_heartland
choose-if: resources >= 1
on-arrival: resources -= 1; ddp_left += 2; ddp_cohesion -= 1; liberal_cooperation -= 1 if liberal_parliament = 1; heartland_coalition_trigger = 1

We have successfully bribed the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>. 

- @prussian_coalition_formation: Negotiate a new Heartland coalition.

@new_prussia_election_oppo
view-if: center_right_coalition_heartland >= 50
on-arrival: in_right_coalition_heartland = 0; in_center_right_coalition_heartland = 1; right_heartland = 1; bourgeois_cooperation += 1; liberal_cooperation += 1

And so we remain.

@new_prussia_election_called
view-if: center_right_coalition_heartland < 50
on-arrival: was_in_weimar_coalition_heartland = 1 if (in_weimar_coalition_heartland == 1 or in_minority_weimar_coalition_heartland == 1); was_in_grand_coalition_heartland = 1 if (in_grand_coalition_heartland == 1 or in_minority_grand_coalition_heartland == 1); in_right_coalition_heartland = 0; in_weimar_coalition_heartland = 0; in_grand_coalition_heartland = 0; in_minority_grand_coalition_heartland = 0; in_popular_front_heartland = 0; in_left_front_heartland = 0; in_marcher_majority_heartland = 0; in_center_right_coalition_heartland = 0; in_far_right_coalition_heartland = 0; in_minority_weimar_coalition_heartland = 0; marcher_heartland = 0; right_heartland = 0; ddp_in_popular_front_heartland = 0; marcher_toleration_heartland = 0; collectivist_goals_seen_heartland = 0
call: set_next_election_time_prussia

New Heartland elections have been set for [+ next_election_month_heartland : month +] [+ next_election_year_heartland + 2365 +].
